1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,963
Thank you for exploring Mutable Dreams, and for telling us what could feel better.

2
00:00:08,963 --> 00:00:12,381
Your feedback is shaping version one point two.

3
00:00:15,417 --> 00:00:20,481
Velvet Keys, Spectral, and Breath expand the palette.

4
00:00:20,481 --> 00:00:29,559
Existing voices have been refined too, with softer contours and more carefully balanced Biomes.

5
00:00:29,559 --> 00:00:38,637
Struck resonators now respond more consistently to equal touches, while keeping their dynamics.

6
00:00:45,667 --> 00:00:50,155
Compose up to thirty-two steps per track.

7
00:00:50,155 --> 00:00:55,301
Shape notes, rests, velocity, gate, and chance.

8
00:00:55,301 --> 00:01:02,746
Record from the keyboard, or generate a phrase and make it your own.

9
00:01:02,746 --> 00:01:08,329
Chord journeys give the harmony a gentle direction.

10
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:19,478
The shared granular cloud gains a little air.

11
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:24,453
Separate track sends let you blend each voice into it.

12
00:01:24,453 --> 00:01:32,098
Improved grain transitions and a more diffuse room help the sounds settle together.

13
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:42,303
The landscapes now respond to your settings, leaving space when the music is sparse.

14
00:01:42,303 --> 00:01:47,942
Brighter lettering and clearer sequence views make editing easier.

15
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:52,215
Hold a function button whenever you need guidance.

16
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:58,710
Save your own Biomes, and keep exploring.

17
00:01:58,710 --> 00:02:05,798
With gratitude to Émilie Gillet, Mutable Instruments, and the open-source community.

18
00:02:05,798 --> 00:02:10,018
Thank you for helping this little instrument grow.
